1. Licensor, material and ownership

"Licensor" means Tyler Alba, operating under the project/developer name
"Albatronic Productions." "NovaCore Material" means original NovaCore source,
binaries, documentation and authored assets expressly made available under this
license, only to the extent Licensor owns or is authorized to license the relevant
rights. Independently licensed components, upstream-derived code, datasets and
other third-party material are excluded. Ownership remains with the respective
rights holders. Source access does not transfer ownership. Rights not expressly
granted are reserved, subject to independently applicable law, platform terms and
other licenses.

An authorized copy is a copy supplied or distribution authorized by Licensor,
or otherwise lawfully obtained under independently applicable rights.

2. Personal use, source inspection and private modification

Subject to these terms, Licensor grants you nonexclusive, worldwide, royalty-free
copyright permission to obtain and retain authorized copies, inspect available
source, build and run NovaCore, and privately modify it for your own personal
play, study, experimentation and hobby use. You may keep private personal copies
and private forks for those purposes. You need not publish your changes.

This personal permission does not authorize general public distribution of
modified or unmodified core/framework material, commercial framework embedding
or sublicensing. Sections 3 and 4 separately permit their stated activities,
including the expressly permitted compensated mod development and monetized
creator activities. Running an authorized NovaCore copy for those activities is
permitted; you need not be a noncommercial creator to exercise section 4.

3. Supported original mods

You may create and use original mod content through interfaces, formats and
distribution methods expressly designated by Licensor as supported for modding.
No interface, SDK, distribution service or continuing technical compatibility is
promised. Private core-source modification does not become a distributable mod.

You may distribute your own original supported-mod files for free through those
supported means. Do not bundle NovaCore core code, binaries or extracted assets
under this permission. Independently licensed material requires its own applicable
permissions. You retain your original mod contributions and may license them to
recipients, without sublicensing NovaCore or changing its terms. Recipients need
their own lawful rights to their NovaCore copy.

Charging users for mod access, downloads, versions or updates requires separate
written authorization, unless a later operative policy expressly permits it.
Genuinely voluntary donations or tips not conditioned on access are permitted;
an access charge does not become a donation merely by being labelled one.
Monetized creator content about a mod is permitted under section 4.

Compensated development of a mod for a client or employer is permitted in itself,
including payment for that development work and delivery of the original mod
files to that client or employer. This does not authorize selling mod access to
users, distributing NovaCore itself, or commercially embedding its framework.
Those activities remain subject to their separate requirements.

The NovaCore Modding Policy 1.0 at docs/legal/MODDING-POLICY.md is an operative
companion recognized for these mod permissions, subject to section 11.

4. Independent creator content and monetization

You may record, reproduce, edit, publish, display, perform and stream independent
content featuring authorized NovaCore use and its original audiovisual output.
This includes videos, Shorts, livestreams, screenshots, reviews and articles,
commentary, tutorials, technical demonstrations, showcases, social posts and
educational content. Critical coverage is included; no favorable opinion is required.

You may monetize that content through advertising, platform revenue sharing,
memberships, subscriptions, sponsorships, donations, tips and sales of independent
content such as a paid review/article. As between you and Licensor, its independent
creator revenue belongs to you; this license imposes no creator revenue share.
Platform, tax and third-party obligations remain separately applicable.

This permission covers inclusion of NovaCore output in your content, not delivery
of runnable NovaCore, core source or standalone extracted assets. It does not
authorize selling, sublicensing or rebranding NovaCore, commercial framework
embedding or a claim to authorship/ownership of NovaCore. You retain your original
creative contributions; featured NovaCore and third-party material retain their
respective ownership.

The NovaCore Creator Content Policy 1.0 at docs/legal/CREATOR-CONTENT-POLICY.md is
an operative companion recognized for these creator permissions, subject to section 11.

