10. Breach, cure, termination and survival

For a curable breach, Licensor will give written notice identifying the breach
and allow 30 days after your receipt to cure it. If cured within that period,
rights will not terminate solely for that cured breach. If it remains uncured
after that period, Licensor may terminate the affected permissions by written
notice. A breach that cannot reasonably be cured may result in immediate
termination by written notice. Notices may be delivered through written contact
channels provided by the recipient; a cure period does not begin before receipt.
After termination, cease activities relying on terminated rights except as
expressly preserved below. Late cure alone does not reinstate rights; reinstatement
requires separate written authorization unless expressly provided by this license.

Creator works lawfully created and already published while compliant may remain
hosted, viewable and monetized after a later unrelated termination. This survival
does not protect never-compliant or infringing works. Materially new works or
releases after termination require valid rights; survival does not restore
terminated software permissions or excuse a separate breach.

Previously lawful, compliant, already-released free supported-mod versions may
remain hosted, downloadable and usable by compliant recipients under the applicable
terms, with their own lawful NovaCore rights. After termination the author has no
permission for new versions, updates or releases without reinstatement or separate
authorization. Never-compliant or infringing material has no survival protection.
A later withdrawal of a supported designation does not by itself revoke the
existing compliant version's permissions or this survival; technical compatibility
and ongoing support are not promised.

Termination does not transfer your original work to Licensor, terminate another
person's independently obtained rights merely by association, alter third-party
licenses, or extinguish rights independently supplied by law. Remedies for
infringement and breaches are preserved. The contribution grant in section 12
survives termination of your permissions to use NovaCore.

