Rights granted under NovaCore Source-Available License 1.0 remain governed by 1.0
unless you affirmatively accept later terms for later or new uses. Website edits
and online policy replacements alone do not retroactively change those rights.
The recognized Creator Content Policy 1.0 and Modding Policy 1.0 share this
license's effective date and may specialize or grant permissions within their
recognized creator/modding scope. Root LICENSE controls an actual conflict unless
it expressly delegates the specific matter; section 3 expressly allows a later
operative policy to permit paid-mod access. A later policy does not silently
withdraw previously granted 1.0 permissions.

NOTICE.md and LICENSING.md explain ownership and licensing. Commercial licensing
information is not itself an agreement. A separate written agreement governs
only the rights and parties actually covered by that agreement.

12. Intentional contributions

For contributions you intentionally submit for inclusion in NovaCore under these
terms, you must hold or have authority to grant the necessary rights. You retain
your copyright; submission is not a copyright assignment. You grant Licensor a
nonexclusive, worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable, royalty-free copyright license
to use, modify, reproduce, maintain, distribute, publicly release and commercially
license your contribution, and sublicense it as part of NovaCore. You also grant
the patent rights you control that are necessary for those acts with your
contribution, alone or in its submitted combination with NovaCore, including
sublicensing as part of NovaCore. This does not grant rights in unrelated inventions
or third-party rights you cannot license.

Identify material subject to other terms and any limits on your authority when
submitting. Do not submit material for inclusion unless sufficient rights for
those uses are available. Material clearly marked as not a contribution and
ordinary discussion not submitted for inclusion are not contributions under
this section. A separately agreed written contribution arrangement controls
its own scope. This section does not retroactively acquire rights in earlier
submissions or make Licensor the owner of another party's work.

